{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Invertible.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.certified_datum_not_barOdd_fixedDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.certified_datum_not_barOdd_fixedDegree","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.lean#L170-L178","doc":"**Headline (fit horn).**  No bar-odd Laurent object has bar-fixed-degree\ncoefficient equal to the certified `{3,4}` DT datum.  Hence reproducing that\ndatum from a bar-odd fibre element cannot come from the (forced) bar-fixed\ndegree — it must come from the non-fixed root-of-unity degrees, which\nbar-oddness leaves free (the Habiro flexibility a derivation may not exploit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.dtDatum_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.dtDatum_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.lean#L167-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.dtDatum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.dtDatum","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.lean#L163-L165","doc":"The certified `q → 0` DT datum of the 5₂ saddle offset: the merged\ndistinguisher's ι-odd value `chiralityOdd 4 3 = 1` (reused, not a fresh number). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.barAntisym_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.barAntisym_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.lean#L155-L159","doc":"**Anti-vacuity.**  A genuinely `q↔q⁻¹`-odd object exists (`g n = n`) and *does*\nhave zero bar-fixed coefficient, so the hypotheses above are satisfiable and the\nnon-selectivity is a real distinction, not a vacuous one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.centring_underdetermined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.centring_underdetermined","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.lean#L138-L151","doc":"**Under-determination.**  The bar-fixed datum does not pin the element: two\n**distinct** bar-odd sequences (`n ↦ n` and `n ↦ 2n`) share the same bar-fixed\ncoefficient `g 0 = 0`.  A fortiori the centring cannot determine *the* saddle\nvector; the discriminating content must come from the non-fixed (root-of-unity)\ndegrees, which bar-oddness leaves free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.q1_centring_nonselective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.q1_centring_nonselective","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.lean#L126-L136","doc":"**The centring is non-selective.**  For any bar-odd `g`, the constraint\n\"vanishes at the bar-fixed degree\" (`g 0 = 0`, the `q = 1` centring) is *already\nimplied* — so `BarAntisym g` and `BarAntisym g ∧ g 0 = 0` are **equivalent**.\nImposing the owner's \"origin-centred at `q = 1`\" on a bar-odd fibre element\nselects **no** element: the property is content-free, hence cannot pick out\n*the knot's* saddle vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.barAntisym_fixedDegree_zero_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.barAntisym_fixedDegree_zero_int","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.lean#L119-L122","doc":"**Bar-fixed-degree vanishing over `ℤ`** (a domain — no `Invertible 2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.barAntisym_fixedDegree_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.barAntisym_fixedDegree_zero","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.lean#L103-L117","doc":"**Bar-fixed-degree vanishing (generic).**  A `q↔q⁻¹`-odd Laurent object has\nzero coefficient at the unique bar-fixed degree `n = 0` (its constant term).\nThis is the coefficient-level mechanism the centring rides on: the bar involution\nacts on degrees by `n ↦ -n`, whose only fixed degree is `n = 0`, so bar-oddness\nforces the constant term to zero.  (Evaluation of the Laurent object at the\ninvolution's fixed points `q = ±1` is a *distinct* statement — not what is\nproved here — so the docstring claims only the `n = 0` coefficient fact.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.barInvolution_fixedDegree_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.barInvolution_fixedDegree_iff","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.lean#L95-L99","doc":"The coefficient action `n ↦ -n` of the bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹` fixes `n`\n**iff** `n = 0`.  The \"centred at `q = 1`\" datum therefore lives at a *single*\ndegree — the `q → 0` / semiclassical one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.BarAntisym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.BarAntisym","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddQOneCentringNonselective.lean#L88-L91","doc":"A Laurent-coefficient sequence `g : ℤ → R` is **q↔q⁻¹-antisymmetric**\n(bar-odd in the modulus): the bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹`, acting on coefficients by\n`n ↦ -n`, negates it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}